'","description":"The Georgia Attorney General blasted LSU in a letter to SEC commissioner Greg Sankey, encouraging sanctions against the Tigers, \"up to and including expulsion.\"","published":"2026-11-18T23:43:26.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/mens-college-basketball/story/_/id/50524054/georgia-ag-asks-sec-take-action-vs-lsu-expulsion","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach and Pete Thamel","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Alabama running back prospect AK Dear no longer with team","description":"Alabama tailback AK Dear, a former four-star prospect who was poised to make an impact before suffering an injury in the summer, is no longer on the team.","published":"2026-11-18T19:16:16.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50523034/alabama-running-back-prospect-ak-dear-no-longer-team","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Judge questions LSU's claims the SEC 'hallucinated' citations","description":"At a hearing Wednesday in the SEC's lawsuit against LSU, a federal judge pushed back on LSU attorneys for using the word \"hallucinated\" in filing.","published":"2026-11-18T22:40:51.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50522883/judge-questions-lsu-claims-sec-hallucinated-citations","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 College Football Playoff National Championship odds","description":"Odds and futures to win the 2027 College Football Playoff National Championship.","published":"2026-11-18T22:17:13.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/47664633/2027-college-football-playoff-national-championship-odds-futures","type":"Story","byline":"Doug Greenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Urban Meyer not a candidate for open Maryland job","description":"Urban Meyer has not spoken to Maryland in any formal capacity about its vacant head coaching position and is not a candidate for the job, sources told ESPN's Pete Thamel on Wednesday.","published":"2026-11-18T18:30:02.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50522632/sources-urban-meyer-not-candidate-open-maryland-job","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Davenport RB Cephus Harris III to enter transfer portal","description":"Davenport's Cephus Harris III, the leading rusher in Division II and a candidate for the Harlon Hill Trophy, plans to enter the transfer portal, he told ESPN.","published":"2026-11-18T17:52:53.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50522473/davenport-rb-cephus-harris-iii-enter-transfer-portal","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Top 25 betting lines: UGA big faves over Gamecocks, Vols slim favorites vs. LSU","description":"This week's odds and FPI predictions for South Carolina-Georgia, Tennessee-LSU and more.","published":"2026-11-18T14:36:40.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/50498153/2026-college-football-week-12-top-25-betting-lines-odds","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Bottom 10 after Week 11: Paying tribute to our founding father","description":"The originator of celebrating football's downtrodden, former Los Angeles columnist Steve Harvey, died last week.","published":"2026-11-18T13:23:01.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50519786/bottom-10-week-11-clemson-steve-harvey","type":"Story","byline":"Ryan McGee","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Take a 360-degree look at college football's iconic rivalry trophies","description":"Whether ancient, animal or absurd, college football's rivalry trophies take many shapes.","published":"2026-11-18T11:39:52.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/feature/story/_/id/50371090/college-football-rivalry-trophies","type":"Eticket","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4685314/sebastian-cheeks","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sebastian_Cheeks"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Sebastian Cheeks","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sebastian_Cheeks","description":"American football player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:38:20Z","intro":"Sebastian Cheeks (born February 6, 2004) is an American college football outside linebacker for the Wisconsin Badgers. He previously played for the North Carolina Tar Heels.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Cheeks attended Evanston Township High School in Evanston, Illinois, where he played linebacker and running back. As a sophomore he recorded two interceptions which he returned for touchdowns over his first four games before suffering a season-ending injury. Cheeks was selected to play in the 2022 All-American Bowl, where he was named the All-American Bowl's Man of the Year. A four-star recruit, he committed to University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Cheeks played the 2022 and 2023 season with North Carolina, recording four tackles over eight games. After the 2023 season, he entered the transfer portal and committed to the University of Wisconsin Madison. In his first year at Wisconsin in 2024, he played in 11 games and had 12 tackles with two sacks. Cheeks started three of 12 games in 2025, recording 24 tackles and three sacks. He returned to Wisconsin as a starter in 2026."}]}}